# replay-sam.rc — the committed sam+samterm scripted-interaction replay
# (15-06 Task 2, D-05: type, edit, write — the two-process pair driven
# end-to-end through the in-guest input files).
#
# Sourced by the baked /lib/trace-session.rc's trace-one AFTER tracesup
# armed the sam tree (sam forks samterm as its own child, so BOTH
# processes plus the libdraw ioproc descendants are born traced — the
# table covers both).  The completion marker rides sam's shell escape:
# the `!echo ...` command is TYPED into samterm's command window via
# kbin, travels the samterm->sam IPC, and sam runs it through /bin/rc
# -c — SAM-SCRIPT-DONE on the serial capture proves both processes'
# loops were reached AND the whole scripted interaction completed
# (D-07).
#
# INPUT CHANNELS — the keyboard is the sam session's deterministic
# floor: samterm is current on its command window (~~sam~~, the top
# fifth of the screen) from startup, and every typed line is forwarded
# to the sam host over the IPC pipe (flushtyping -> outcmd).  The
# first boot drove the B3 menu-New + sweep path instead and measured
# it dead on this venue: the menu's New left samterm's `which` unset
# pending the host's Hcurrent, so the sweep's B3 press re-opened the
# menu (the +1px menuhit warps on the capture pin it) and the typed
# text fell through to the command window.  One B1 click low in the
# command window keeps keyboard focus there without relying on any
# layer state; /dev/mousein is RELATIVE (home-clamp then known deltas,
# the replay-rio.rc discipline).
#
# The interaction set (D-05's floor for sam), one kbin line each —
# every line is a SINGLE-LINE command (send -> host executes -> Hunlock
# -> next line): the second boot measured the multi-line `a` insert
# mode dead on this venue (samterm's kbd channel blocks on the
# full-channel/`kbdblock` mask pending host Hunlocks that never arrive
# mid-command — the ioproc's reads stop on the capture), while every
# single-line command in both boots completed its full round trip:
#   - TYPE text into the FILE: `a/text/` inserts the typed runes into
#     the current file (through samterm's loop, over the IPC, into
#     sam's buffer)
#   - EDIT: `,s/replay/REPLAY/` substitutes in the file
#   - WRITE: `w` writes /tmp/sam-replay.txt (the ramfs scratch; B
#     loaded it, so the file is named and w is a plain write)
#   - the marker shell escape, then `q` (sam exits; samterm follows)

# 0. the file sam was STARTED with (the session driver seeds it before
#    the launch): argv-loaded inside the startup handshake, so no
#    mid-session B/load exchange (see the session-driver note)

# 1. focus the command window: B1 click LOW inside it (below the text
#    lines — the selection lands at the end of the command text, so
#    typed commands append after the last output; a first click on a
#    non-current layer only makes it current)
echo 'M -5000 -5000 0 0' > '#m/mousein'
sleep 1
echo 'M 512 140 0 0' > '#m/mousein'
sleep 1
echo 'M 0 0 1 0' > '#m/mousein'
sleep 1
echo 'M 0 0 0 0' > '#m/mousein'
sleep 2

# 2. the command ladder: create the file entry, type into it, edit,
#    write, mark, quit — each line a kbin write, samterm forwards on
#    newline; generous sleeps after the load-bearing commands (the
#    venue's samterm input machinery is pacing-sensitive right after a
#    file exchange — measured across five bring-up boots)
echo 'B /tmp/sam-replay.txt' > '#c/kbin'
sleep 6
# the B1 click resets the cmd window's dot to EMPTY: a command's reply
# leaves a non-empty dot, and samterm's type() then cuts the selection
# and returns WITHOUT consuming the pending runes (the observed stall
# shape — the first typed line after a file command is never consumed)
echo 'M -5000 -5000 0 0' > '#m/mousein'
sleep 1
echo 'M 512 148 0 0' > '#m/mousein'
sleep 1
echo 'M 0 0 1 0' > '#m/mousein'
sleep 1
echo 'M 0 0 0 0' > '#m/mousein'
sleep 2
echo 'a/hello from the 15-06 sam replay/' > '#c/kbin'
sleep 4
echo ',s/replay/REPLAY/' > '#c/kbin'
sleep 4
echo 'w' > '#c/kbin'
sleep 4
echo '!echo SAM-SCRIPT-DONE > ''#c/cons''' > '#c/kbin'
sleep 3
echo q > '#c/kbin'
sleep 3
